","year":"1948"},{"id":"3177_You_and_Your_Friends_E01756_02_21_29_00","mp4":"3177_You_and_Your_Friends_E01756_02_21_29_00.mp4","moov":404439,"duration":476,"title":"You and Your Friends","year":"1946"},{"id":"FindingY1940","mp4":"FindingY1940.mp4","moov":983050,"duration":1159,"title":"Finding Your Life's Work","year":"1940"},{"id":"0643_Driving_Tips_Part_1_04_37_28_00","mp4":"0643_Driving_Tips_Part_1_04_37_28_00.mp4","moov":488460,"duration":575,"title":"Driving Tips, Part 1","year":"1958"},{"id":"0042_Capitalism_E00102_18_20_52_00","mp4":"0042_Capitalism_E00102_18_20_52_00-0010.mp4","moov":488147,"duration":575,"title":"Capitalism","year":"1948"},{"id":"0838_Dont_Get_Angry_11_11_58_11","mp4":"0838_Dont_Get_Angry_11_11_58_11.mp4","moov":580061,"duration":683,"title":"Don't Get Angry","year":"1953"},{"id":"200323_The_Dangerous_Stranger_color","mp4":"200323_The_Dangerous_Stranger_color_master.intros.mp4","moov":420649,"duration":607,"title":"The Dangerous Stranger","year":"1977"},{"id":"2318_As_the_Twig_Is_Bent_02_10_10_00","mp4":"2318_As_the_Twig_Is_Bent_02_10_10_00.mp4","moov":555829,"duration":655,"title":"As the Twig Is Bent...","year":"1944"},{"id":"0013_How_to_Use_Classroom_Films_E00474_13_29_45_00","mp4":"0013_How_to_Use_Classroom_Films_E00474_13_29_45_00.mp4","moov":736399,"duration":868,"title":"How to Use Classroom Films","year":"1963"},{"id":"0022_Film_Research_Learning_22_00_34_00","mp4":"0022_Film_Research_Learning_22_00_34_00.mp4","moov":668661,"duration":788,"title":"Film Research & Learning...","year":"1956"},{"id":"0021_Darkness_Before_the_Dawn_The_Pride_of_Judea_Story_21_34_09_00","mp4":"0021_Darkness_Before_the_Dawn_The_Pride_of_Judea_Story_21_34_09_00.mp4","moov":1083329,"duration":1277,"title":"Darkness Before the Dawn: The \"Pride of Judea\" Story","year":"1955"},{"id":"Wild_at_the_Wheel","mp4":"Wild_at_the_Wheel_master.intros.mp4","moov":442270,"duration":643,"title":"Wild at the Wheel","year":"1970"},{"id":"200516_Live_and_Learn","mp4":"Live_and_Learn_master.intros.mp4","moov":522511,"duration":758,"title":"Live and Learn","year":"1951"},{"id":"200464_The_Dangerous_Stranger","mp4":"200464_Dangerous_Stranger.intros.mp4","moov":432667,"duration":624,"title":"The Dangerous Stranger (First Edition)","year":"1949"}],"bumps":[{"id":"hr-001","slides":[{"text":"these films were made by adults"},{"text":"who had never successfully spoken to a teenager."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-002","slides":[{"text":"the projector cart had one wobbly wheel."},{"text":"every school. same wheel."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-003","slides":[{"text":"the guidance counselors who ordered these films"},{"text":"were absolutely certain they worked."},{"text":"the kids who watched them"},{"text":"were absolutely certain they didn't."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-004","slides":[{"text":"coronet films made over a thousand of these."},{"text":"not one teenager changed their behavior."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-005","slides":[{"text":"every kid in these films sits up too straight."},{"text":"that was the whole direction."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-006","slides":[{"text":"\"are you popular?\" came out in 1947."},{"text":"the answer was always no."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-007","slides":[{"text":"the narrator solved every teenage problem"},{"text":"by suggesting you try harder."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-008","slides":[{"text":"the teacher pulled the shades down,"},{"text":"threaded the projector,"},{"text":"pressed play,"},{"text":"sat at her desk,"},{"text":"and graded papers for twenty minutes."},{"text":"the film was the lesson plan."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-009","slides":[{"text":"\"what to do on a date\" suggested miniature golf."},{"text":"specifically."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-010","slides":[{"text":"the 1950s had a film for every social situation."},{"text":"none of the social situations were real."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-011","slides":[{"text":"the good kid in the film always makes the right choice."},{"text":"nobody in the audience ever did."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-012","slides":[{"text":"someone in a school district office"},{"text":"watched a 16mm film catalog"},{"text":"the way other people watch netflix."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-013","slides":[{"text":"the films always end with the teenager smiling."},{"text":"that was the proof it worked."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-014","slides":[{"text":"the bulb in the projector cost more"},{"text":"than the film rental."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-015","slides":[{"text":"in 1949, coronet films released"},{"text":"\"how to be well groomed.\""},{"text":"it ran eleven minutes."},{"text":"they thought eleven minutes was enough."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-016","slides":[{"text":"every problem in these films"},{"text":"is caused by not listening to an adult."},{"text":"the adults wrote the films."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-017","slides":[{"text":"the bad kid in the film"},{"text":"is always the most interesting person on screen."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-018","slides":[{"text":"the narrator has never met a teenager."},{"text":"you can tell by the way he says \"teenager.\""},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-019","slides":[{"text":"coronet films was founded in 1934 in chicago."},{"text":"by 1950 they were the largest producer of educational films in america."},{"text":"their catalog covered everything:"},{"text":"dating, hygiene, manners, citizenship, friendship, posture."},{"text":"they made over a thousand films about how to be a person."},{"text":"they went out of business in 1977."},{"text":"the teenagers outlasted them."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-020","slides":[{"text":"the school district bought these in bulk."},{"text":"like paper towels."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-021","slides":[{"text":"in the films, the unpopular kid becomes popular"},{"text":"by being more polite."},{"text":"in real life, the unpopular kid"},{"text":"just waited until college."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-022","slides":[{"text":"the actors in these films were adults"},{"text":"playing teenagers."},{"text":"the teenagers in the audience"},{"text":"were playing dead."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-023","slides":[{"text":"the projector broke more often than it worked."},{"text":"nobody was upset about this."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-024","slides":[{"text":"\"how to say no\" was a real film."},{"text":"twelve minutes long."},{"text":"the answer was: say no."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-025","slides":[{"text":"the guidance counselor's office"},{"text":"had a poster about attitude"},{"text":"and a locked filing cabinet"},{"text":"full of these film catalogs."},{"text":"that filing cabinet was their whole strategy."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-026","slides":[{"text":"every film opens with a teenager who has a problem."},{"text":"the problem is always that they're a teenager."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-027","slides":[{"text":"the recommended solution to peer pressure"},{"text":"was a firm handshake"},{"text":"and a clear sense of purpose."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-028","slides":[{"text":"somebody's job was to write these."},{"text":"they went home at five o'clock"},{"text":"and told their family they worked in education."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-029","slides":[{"text":"the teenager in the film has a nice house,"},{"text":"two parents,"},{"text":"a dog,"},{"text":"and one manageable problem."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-030","slides":[{"text":"coronet films believed"},{"text":"that good posture"},{"text":"was a personality trait."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-031","slides":[{"text":"the classroom was dark."},{"text":"the projector was loud."},{"text":"the film was about sharing."},{"text":"three kids in the back were asleep."},{"text":"the system worked exactly as designed."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-032","slides":[{"text":"the films assumed every teenager"},{"text":"was one lecture away from being fixed."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-033","slides":[{"text":"there's a scene in every one of these"},{"text":"where a teenager stares out a window"},{"text":"and thinks about their choices."},{"text":"the window was in a studio in chicago."},{"text":"there was nothing outside it."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-034","slides":[{"text":"the film said ask your parents."},{"text":"your parents said ask your teacher."},{"text":"your teacher put on another film."},{"text":"homeroom."}]},{"id":"hr-035","slides":[{"text":"up next: more teenagers learning valuable lessons"},{"text":"they'll forget by lunch."},{"text":"homeroom."}]}],"audio":[{"filename":"slowerpace-night-of-pleasures.mp3","title":"Night Of Pleasures","artist":"Slowerpace","url":"https://slowerpace.bandcamp.com/track/night-of-pleasures","license":"by"},{"filename":"slowerpace-maison-close.mp3","title":"Maison Close","artist":"Slowerpace","url":"https://slowerpace.bandcamp.com/track/maison-close","license":"by"},{"filename":"slowerpace-vip-pass.mp3","title":"Vip Pass","artist":"Slowerpace","url":"https://slowerpace.bandcamp.com/track/vip-pass","license":"by"},{"filename":"slowerpace-pure-delight.mp3","title":"Pure Delight","artist":"Slowerpace","url":"https://slowerpace.bandcamp.com/track/pure-delight","license":"by"},{"filename":"slowerpace-pulsing-colors.mp3","title":"Pulsing Colors","artist":"Slowerpace","url":"https://slowerpace.bandcamp.com/track/pulsing-colors","license":"by"},{"filename":"slowerpace-desire-suite.mp3","title":"Desire Suite","artist":"Slowerpace","url":"https://slowerpace.bandcamp.com/track/desire-suite","license":"by"},{"filename":"slowerpace-the-last-cigarette.mp3","title":"The Last Cigarette","artist":"Slowerpace","url":"https://slowerpace.bandcamp.com/track/the-last-cigarette","license":"by"},{"filename":"purrplecat-crossroads.mp3","title":"Crossroads","artist":"Purrplecat","url":"https://purrplec